{"ts":"2026-09-10T22:20:49.814Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"3a51a1fe5204a56374236921","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.268","source":"probe"}},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-10T22:20:49.814Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-09-10T22:20:49.780Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-09-10T22:20:49.780Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Pins advanced: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.7 to 2026.9.10, pm-ops 2026.9.7 to 2026.9.9. Greptile and CodeRabbit both observed that the bump closed seven fail-open cases without leaving anything in this repository that would notice if they returned, and that the clean-corpus claim had no structured test behind it. Both are correct. Added two tests to test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts: the seven constructions are run through auditPublishAttestation from the installed pm-ops and each must be refused, plus a positive control asserting a readable --provenance binding still passes. The guard asserts behaviour rather than a version number, so it also fails against a regressed release numbered above any floor. Revert-check: with pm-ops downgraded to 2026.9.7 the guard goes RED naming the nonliteral-overwrite construction while the control stays green; restoring 2026.9.9 returns the suite to 167 of 167. The 38-case corpus itself stays in the private companion because it is fleet infrastructure, so the linked test names the local guard, which is the part that is runnable here."}],"before_hash":"a9828252a849685d30fb5123503d6eb2512f458713e5461c4c6cd9f14ac9be2a","after_hash":"b1a41bf98f85c12d87c788a92acee3a32f0c31faad96b7d70270f932c3c8331d","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"39e9c08962b2b96c425f63ba83c25a8dd74295bbf446864c8b1ea7daa020080c"}
